    {# ===================== 4 — POSITIONING =====================
      One line, centred, with nothing to click. This is the only section on the
      page with no next step in it, which is the point: it is the argument, and
      an argument that ends in a button reads as a pitch.
    #}
    <section class="section section--paper hp-position" id="positioning" aria-labelledby="hp-position-line">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hp-position__inner">
          <h2 class="statement hp-position__line" id="hp-position-line">Water treatment isn't optional. <span class="em">Neither is doing it properly.</span></h2>
          <p class="hp-position__body">Twenty years of bespoke systems for clients who need current compliance evidence, not just clean water. Football grounds, pharmaceutical sites, hospices and landed estates. The standard we work to is the standard your inspector expects.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# ===================== 5 — COVERAGE =====================
      WHERE WE WORK, SAID AS A MAP RATHER THAN AS A SENTENCE. This replaces the
      typographic sectors list that used to sit here: the client asked for
      sectors removed from the site completely (11/08/26), and the honest
      answer to "do you come to me" was always the geography, not a list of
      industries.

      The site's own component, the same one that closes /about/ and every
      service page, so the coverage claim is made in one place and one way.
      Without GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY it falls back to the keyless embed and still
      draws the South East; the key only buys the shaded counties.
    #}
    {% include "coverage-band.njk" %}

    {# ===================== 6 — SELECTED WORK =====================
      A CAROUSEL OF EVERY STUDY, one at a time: photograph left, the account
      right. It used to be Cowdray alone, on the argument that one job told
      properly beats three at card size. That still holds per slide; the
      carousel just lets the other seven be told the same way, without eight
      screens of page. Cowdray leads, as the one named client.

      Arrows sit out in the page gutters, level with the photograph, and step
      one study at a time (carousel.js). Below 900px they go and the track is a
      swipe with dots. With no JavaScript it is a plain snapping scroller.

      Slides carry the first body paragraph only. The full write-ups run to
      three paragraphs, and a slide that changes height by 200px on every
      click makes the section below it jump.
    #}
    {% set serviceNames = {
      "private-water-supplies": "Private water supplies",
      "design-install": "Design and install",
      "water-hygiene": "Water hygiene",
      "servicing": "Servicing"
    } %}
    {% set cowdray = {
      id: "cowdray",
      title: "Cowdray Estate, <span class='em'>a private supply serving multiple properties.</span>",
      location: "Midhurst, West Sussex",
      services: ["private-water-supplies"],
      body: ["Cowdray needed a reliable, high-volume private supply serving multiple properties and estate operations. We surveyed two potential borehole sites, specified the higher-yield source, and installed a treatment system built around iron and manganese reduction, pH correction to stop the water corroding pipework, and UV sterilisation."],
      highlight: "Running continuously since 2023, and passing UKAS-accredited testing every year.",
      image: "/assets/img-9257.webp",
      imageAlt: "A red brick water tower beside a barn with solar panels, with an Invicta van on the drive."
    } %}
    {% set slides = [cowdray].concat(caseStudies) %}
    <section class="section section--paper hp-work" id="selected-work" aria-labelledby="hp-work-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hp-work__head">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow hp-eyebrow">Selected work</p>
            <h2 class="statement hp-work__title" id="hp-work-title">Supplies we’ve designed, <span class="em">installed and looked after.</span></h2>
          </div>
          <p class="hp-work__count" aria-hidden="true"><span data-cases-current>01</span> / {% if slides.length < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ slides.length }}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="hp-cases" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Case studies">
          <button type="button" class="hp-cases__arrow hp-cases__arrow--prev" data-cc-prev aria-label="Previous case study"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg></button>
          <button type="button" class="hp-cases__arrow hp-cases__arrow--next" data-cc-next aria-label="Next case study"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></button>

          <div class="hp-cases__track">
            {% for c in slides %}
            {% set svc = c.services[0] %}
            <article class="hp-case" role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="{{ loop.index }} of {{ slides.length }}">
              <figure class="hp-case__media">
                <img src="{{ c.image or '/assets/img-0428.webp' }}" alt="{{ c.imageAlt }}" width="1536" height="1024" loading="{{ 'eager' if loop.first else 'lazy' }}" decoding="async">
              </figure>
              <div class="hp-case__copy">
                {# The SERVICE half of this line is gone. It said "Private
                   water supplies" directly above a button saying "More on
                   private water supplies", so the eyebrow's second half was
                   the same words twice, four lines apart. The place stays:
                   for a regional business "Midhurst, West Sussex" is the one
                   thing here a reader cannot get from anything else on the
                   slide, and it is doing real work. #}
                <p class="hp-case__meta"><span>{{ c.location }}</span></p>
                <h3 class="hp-case__title">{{ c.title | safe }}</h3>
                <p class="hp-case__body">{{ c.body[0] }}</p>
                {% if c.highlight %}<p class="hp-case__highlight">{{ c.highlight }}</p>{% endif %}
                <p class="hp-case__link">
                  <a class="btn-line" href="/services/{{ svc }}/">More on {{ serviceNames[svc] | lower }} <span class="btn-line__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></a>
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>

          <div class="hp-cases__dots" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a case study"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# ===================== 6b — IN THEIR WORDS =====================
      Three real clients, anonymised to the place, as Stefan promised them
      (see _data/testimonials.js). Straight after the one case study, so the
      page goes from our account of a job to the clients' account of theirs.

      NOT A CAROUSEL ON DESKTOP. Three quotes fit on one screen, and a slider
      would hide two of them behind a control to show fewer at once. The
      longest, most specific quote takes the large card; the other two stack
      beside it, so uneven lengths read as a hierarchy rather than as three
      boxes with ragged bottoms. On a phone the same three become a swipe row
      with dots (nav.js TRACKS), which is where a carousel earns its keep.
    #}
    <section class="section section--light hp-voices" id="testimonials" aria-labelledby="hp-voices-title">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow hp-eyebrow">In their words</p>
        <h2 class="statement hp-voices__title" id="hp-voices-title">Don’t just take our word for it.</h2>

        <div class="hp-voices__grid">
          {% for t in testimonials %}
          <figure class="voice{% if t.feature %} voice--feature{% endif %}">
            <svg class="voice__mark" viewBox="0 0 32 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 24V14.4C0 6.2 4.3 1.4 12.2 0l1.4 3.1C9.2 4.6 7 7.4 6.8 11.2H13V24H0zm19 0V14.4C19 6.2 23.3 1.4 31.2 0l1.4 3.1c-4.4 1.5-6.6 4.3-6.8 8.1H32V24H19z"/></svg>
            <blockquote class="voice__quote">
              {% if t.pull %}<p class="voice__pull">{{ t.pull }}</p>{% endif %}
              {% for para in t.quote %}<p>{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption class="voice__by">
              <span class="voice__who">Private water supply, near {{ t.place }}</span>
              <span class="voice__scope">{{ t.scope }}</span>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {# ===================== 7 — CREDENTIALS =====================
      THE QUALIFYING MOMENT. Everything above is what we do; this is the answer
      to "can you actually be put on our approved list". The question stays
      stuck to the top of the screen while the six answers scroll past it,
      because they are a list you scan rather than read.

      A description list, not headings: these are terms and their definitions,
      and keeping them out of the heading outline leaves the page with one H1
      and one H2 per section, which is what it should have.
    #}
    <section class="section hp-creds" id="credentials" aria-labelledby="hp-creds-title">
      <div class="container hp-creds__grid">
        <div class="hp-creds__aside">
          <p class="eyebrow hp-eyebrow">Credentials</p>
